||| Build-time selection of the (device, dtype) pair that examples
||| target. Generated from this template by the Makefile rule at
||| `Makefile`'s BUILDCONFIG_IDR target, which observes `PRIMARY` +
||| `MLX_DEVICE` + `TORCH_DEVICE` at build time and substitutes the
||| chosen tags into this template via sed.
|||
||| Selection matrix (PRIMARY × hw-device env → ExampleExecutor, ExampleDType):
|||
|||   tape, *                     → TapeExecutor,              F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cpu      → TorchExecutor TCpu,        F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=mps      → TorchExecutor TMps,        F32
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cuda     → TorchExecutor (TCuda 0),   F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=cpu          → MlxExecutor MCpu,          F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=gpu          → MlxExecutor MGpu,          F32
|||
||| TMps + F64 deliberately doesn't exist — libtorch rejects F64 at
||| MPS tensor construction. mlx GPU is F32-only too (Metal dropped
||| F64 support in mlx 0.31). All other cells stay F64 for parity
||| with the historical references.
|||
||| Idris-2 cannot drive type-level selection from a runtime env var —
||| types are fixed at elaboration time, before `main`. The generated
||| `BuildConfig.idr` is in `.gitignore`.
|||
||| Do not edit `BuildConfig.idr` directly — your changes will be
||| clobbered on the next build. Edit this `.in` file instead.
module BuildConfig

import public Executor
import public Executor.Tape
import public Executor.Torch
import public Executor.Mlx

||| Executor tag examples target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
ExampleExecutor : Type
ExampleExecutor = @DEVICE@

||| DType examples target. See the Selection matrix in the module
||| docstring.
public export
ExampleDType : DType
ExampleDType = @DTYPE@
